cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize RENA in your research, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "RENA Research Team"
    given-names: "Independent Audit Group"
title: "RENA: A Controlled Multi-Turn Evaluation Protocol for AI Unlearning and Privacy Audits"
version: 2.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
url: "https://github.com/rena-project/rena_v22"
keywords:
  - machine unlearning
  - privacy audits
  - behavioral suppression
  - large language models
  - AI security
  - causal attribution
abstract: >
  RENA is a rigorous evaluation protocol and auditing engine for machine unlearning
  and privacy compliance in Large Language Models. It formalizes a 3-group experimental
  architecture combining baseline-retrievability gating, unexposed reference controls,
  counterfactual exposure baselines, and multi-turn conversational probing to uncover
  suppressed-but-retained latent knowledge.
